    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0504" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">803.24/1048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-21T19:00:00+03:00">April 21, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 21—6:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>819. My 786, April 16, 7 p.m.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d537-f1"/> The [Chinese
                    Ambassador made the statement?] that he has now received “a satisfactory reply”
                    to his inquiry of the Soviet Government concerning continued assistance to
                    Chiang Kai-shek. As there were Axis diplomats present at our meeting I did not
                    press him for details.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
